## Memory protocol

Before work, read the constitution, current state, decision summary, active chunk,
risks, and next action. After work, update status, chunk evidence, decisions, risks,
technical debt, progress, current state, session handoff, and exactly one next action.

## Invariants

- Repository memory is authoritative; chat history is never required.
- Facts, decisions, assumptions, proposals, and superseded information are labelled.
- Every material statement links to evidence or an owning artifact.
- Machine state and narrative state change together.
- Secrets, credentials, personal data, and transient logs do not enter memory.

## Retention

Preserve decisions and completion evidence. Summarise stale operational detail and
link to version control rather than allowing files to grow without bound.

